{"title":"Aluminium PFC","markdown":{"headingText":"Aluminium PFC","headingAttr":{"id":"sec-aluminum","classes":[],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n`apps/aluminumNew` — a compact PFC application in the same family as\n@sec-tungsten, parameterised for aluminium and built around a moving frame.\n\n## Physical setting\n\nThe same phase-field crystal picture as @sec-tungsten: a conserved periodic\ndensity whose minima are lattice sites. The differences are the equation of\nstate, an FCC seeding initial condition (`seed_grid_fcc`), and a moving-frame\nformulation aimed at directional solidification, where the interesting physics\nis a front travelling through the domain rather than a bulk relaxation.\n\n## Governing equations\n\nConserved PFC dynamics, as in @eq-w-dyn:\n\n$$\n\\partial_t \\psi \\;=\\; \\nabla^2 \\frac{\\delta F}{\\delta \\psi}.\n$$\n\nThe free energy has the same structure as @eq-w-energy — a quadratic\ncorrelation term plus a local polynomial in $\\psi$ and the mean-field density\n— with the aluminium coefficients $\\bar p_2,\\bar p_3,\\bar p_4$ and\n$\\bar q_{20},\\dots,\\bar q_{40}$.\n\n## Spectral formulation\n\n$$\nL(k) \\;=\\; u\\,C(k), \\qquad M_{\\mathrm{nl}}(k) \\;=\\; u ,\n\\qquad u = k_{\\mathrm{lap}} = -|\\mathbf{k}|^2 .\n$$ {#eq-al-symbol}\n\nAlongside $C(k)$ the model carries a separate **correlation kernel** $P(k)$\napplied to the density each step. The pointwise nonlinearity is therefore a\nfunction of four arguments rather than two,\n\n$$\nN \\;=\\; N\\big(\\psi,\\ \\psi_{\\mathrm{MF}},\\ (P*\\psi),\\ T_{\\mathrm{var}}(x,t)\\big),\n$$ {#eq-al-nl}\n\nwhere $(P*\\psi)$ is the kernel-filtered density — a convolution in real space,\nhence a multiply in reciprocal space — and $T_{\\mathrm{var}}$ is the imposed\ntemperature field.\n\n## Moving frame and thermal drive\n\nThe temperature varies in space and time as a travelling profile,\n\n$$\nT_{\\mathrm{var}}(x,t) \\;=\\;\n  T_0 + G_{\\mathrm{grid}}\\big(x - x_{\\mathrm{initial}} - V_{\\mathrm{grid}}\\,t\\big),\n$$ {#eq-al-temp}\n\nclamped between `T_min` and `T_max`. A gradient $G_{\\mathrm{grid}}$ pulled\nthrough the domain at speed $V_{\\mathrm{grid}}$ is the standard\ndirectional-solidification setup: the front settles at the position where the\nlocal temperature matches the interface condition, and then travels with the\ngradient. Setting $G_{\\mathrm{grid}}=0$ recovers an isothermal run at\n`T_const`.\n\n## Solution strategy\n\nETD1 as in @eq-etd1, dealiased, with the mean-field filter and the correlation\nkernel evaluated as reciprocal-space multiplies. Two transforms per step plus\nthe kernel application.\n\n## Verification\n\n* **Regression.** Pinned checksums for the shipped case across CPU and GPU\n  builds.\n* **Schema.** JSON round-trip and range validation on every parameter.\n\nLike @sec-tungsten this model has no closed-form reference; coverage is\nregression and schema rather than analytical.\n\n## Binaries and inputs\n\n`aluminum_etd` (CPU), `aluminum_etd_cuda`, `aluminum_etd_hip`. Preset\n`inputs_json/smoke.json`, plus `aluminumNew.json`.\n\n## Scalability\n\nNot measured. The application shares the spectral ETD stack with\n@sec-tungsten, so its per-step cost is expected to track the tungsten curve at\nequal grid size, but that has not been verified and no curve is reported here.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"ou